# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Astro, then read by
# Pages at the edge. Astro itself never sees this file, so `astro dev` will 404
# on these paths — that is expected, not a bug.
#
# 302, not 301: these are convenience aliases for the Sanity Studio, which is a
# hosted URL that could move. A 301 is cached hard by browsers and would keep
# sending people to a dead host long after the redirect was corrected.
#
# Cloudflare docs: "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not
# an asset matches the incoming request" — so these win over any built page at
# the same path.

/admin      https://auristate.sanity.studio  302
/admin/*    https://auristate.sanity.studio/:splat  302
/studio     https://auristate.sanity.studio  302
/studio/*   https://auristate.sanity.studio/:splat  302
